<title>BELGIUM: German, French EMU plans cleared in EU committee.</title>
<headline>German, French EMU plans cleared in EU committee.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Monetary Committee approved on Wednesday French and German economic convergence plans to qualify for the European Union's single currency, a monetary source said.</p>
<p>The plans will now be forwarded to EU finance ministers who are expected to approve them at their next scheduled meeting on March 17, the source said. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
